WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.310
- [Woman] This video is sponsored

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.770
by the American Lung Cancer
Screening Initiative.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.450
Lung cancer is the leading cause

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.490
of cancer related death in the world.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.200
But lung cancer screening can save lives.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.083
Click the link below to learn more.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.930
Every time you smoke a cigarette

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.370
toxic gases pass into your lungs,

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.740
then into your bloodstream.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.763
Where they spread to
every organ in your body.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.960
A cigarette is made using the tobacco leaf

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.143
which contains nicotine and
a variety of other compounds.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.470
As the tobacco and compounds burn,

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:48.320
they release thousands
of dangerous chemicals,

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.663
including over 40 known to cause cancer.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.980
Cigarette smoke contains
the poisonous gases,

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.970
carbon monoxide and nitrogen oxide,

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:00.580
as well as trace amounts

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.573
of cancer causing radioactive particles.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.370
All forms of tobacco are dangerous,

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.930
including cigars, pipes
and smokeless tobacco,

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.283
such as chewing tobacco and snuff.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.360
Nicotine is an addictive
chemical in tobacco.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.500
After you inhale tobacco smoke,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.190
nicotine flows through the
bloodstream to your brain,

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.843
where it induces a pleasurable feeling.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.680
When you repeatedly expose
your brain to nicotine

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.610
it becomes desensitized.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.623
Making you crave more and more
nicotine just to feel normal.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.460
Smoking causes death.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.490
People who smoke typically die

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.210
at an earlier age than non-smokers.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.080
In fact, one of every five
deaths in the United States

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.283
is linked to cigarette smoking.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.350
If you smoke your risk
of major health problems

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:04.540
increases dramatically
including heart disease,

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:09.270
heart attack, stroke, lung cancer,

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.933
and death from chronic
obstructive pulmonary disease.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.020
Smoking causes cardiovascular disease.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:29.880
When nicotine flows through
your adrenal glands,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.453
it stimulates the release of epinephrine.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.113
A hormone that raises your blood pressure.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.720
In addition, nicotine and carbon monoxide

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.403
can damage the lining of the
inner walls in your arteries.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.910
Fatty deposits called plaque

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.330
can build up at these injury sites

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:55.140
and become large enough
to narrow the arteries

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.340
and severely reduce blood flow

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.203
resulting in a condition
called atherosclerosis.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.110
In coronary artery disease,

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:10.110
atherosclerosis narrows the
arteries that supply the heart

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.810
which reduces the supply of
oxygen to your heart muscle,

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.363
increasing your risk for a heart attack.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.460
Smoking also raises your
risk for blood clots

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.193
because it causes platelets in
your blood to clump together.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:32.010
Smoking increases your risk for
peripheral vascular disease,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.170
in which atherosclerotic plaques

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:37.543
block the large arteries
in your arms and legs.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.500
Smoking can also cause an
abdominal aortic aneurysm.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.510
Which is a swelling or
weakening of your aorta

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.603
where it runs through your abdomen.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:58.170
Smoking damages two main
parts of your lungs.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:02.050
Your airways also called bronchial tubes

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.883
and small air sacs called alveoli.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.000
With each breath,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.440
air travels down your
windpipe called the trachea

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.703
and enters your lungs
through your bronchial tubes.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:21.100
Air then moves into
thousands of tiny alveoli.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.660
Where oxygen from the air
moves into your bloodstream

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:28.230
and the waste product carbon dioxide

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.133
moves out of your bloodstream.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.610
Tiny hair-like projections called cilia

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.240
line bronchial tubes

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.663
and sweep harmful substances
out of your lungs.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.890
Cigarette smoke irritates the lining

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.190
of your bronchial tubes,

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:51.023
causing them to swell and make mucus.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.660
Cigarette smoke also slows
the movement of your cilia

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:00.683
causing some of the smoke and
mucus to stay in your lungs.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:05.820
While you are sleeping
some of the cilia recover

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.920
and start pushing more pollutants

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.083
and mucus out of your lungs.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.300
When you wake up your body
attempts to expel this material

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.060
by coughing repeatedly.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.763
A condition known as smoker's cough.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.830
Over time, chronic bronchitis develops

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:26.020
as your cilia stop working.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.300
Your airways become clogged
with scars and mucus

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.740
and breathing becomes difficult.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.363
Your lungs are now more
vulnerable to further disease.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.840
Cigarette smoke also damages your alveoli,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.090
making it harder for
oxygen and carbon dioxide

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.863
to exchange with your blood.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.360
Over time so little oxygen
can reach your blood

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.600
that you may develop emphysema.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.870
A condition in which you
must gasp for every breath

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.330
and wear an oxygen tube under your nose

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.713
in order to breathe.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:05.030
Chronic bronchitis and emphysema
are collectively called

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.023
chronic obstructive
pulmonary disease or COPD.

00:06:09.505 --> 00:06:13.370
COPD is a gradual loss
of the ability to breathe

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.443
for which there is no cure.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.770
Cigarette smoke contains

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:28.430
at least 40 cancer causing
substances called carcinogens,

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:33.430
including cyanide, formaldehyde,
benzene and ammonia.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.310
In your body, healthy cells grow,

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.830
make new cells, then die.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:46.900
Genetic material inside
each cell called DNA

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.673
directs this process.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.560
If you smoke, toxic chemicals

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.773
can damage the DNA in your healthy cells.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.150
As a result, your damaged cells

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:03.190
create new unhealthy cells.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.090
Which grow out of control

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.833
and may spread to other
parts of your body.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.970
The most common cancer in
the world is lung cancer,

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:17.003
with over a million new
cases diagnosed every year.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.120
Harmful chemicals in cigarettes

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.900
can cause cancer in
other parts of your body,

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:28.060
such as in the blood and bone marrow,

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:33.060
mouth, larynx, throat, esophagus, stomach,

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:41.510
pancreas, kidney, bladder,
uterus and cervix.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.513
Smoking can cause infertility
in both men and women.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:01.580
If a woman is pregnant and
smokes during pregnancy,

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.450
she exposes her baby to the
cigarette's poisonous chemicals

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:09.190
causing a greater risk
of low birth weight,

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:13.970
miscarriage, preterm delivery, stillbirth,

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.983
infant death and sudden
infant death syndrome.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:24.690
Smoking is also dangerous if
a mother is breastfeeding.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:28.780
Nicotine passes to the
baby through breast milk

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:33.500
and can cause restlessness,
rapid heartbeat,

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:38.500
vomiting, interrupted sleep or diarrhea.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.050
Other health effects of smoking

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:45.670
include low bone density

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.230
and increased risk for
hip fracture among women,

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:53.430
gum disease often leading
to tooth loss and surgery,

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.270
immune system dysfunction
and delayed wound healing

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.593
and sexual impotence in men.

